sentences.l:
and he stood, then, having sprung up, and saw the Trojans and Achaeans,
some being stirred up, others throwing them into confusion from behind,
Argives, and among them Poseidon the lord;

sentences.t:
ἦ οὐ μέμνῃ ὅτε τ’ ἐκρέμω ὑψόθεν, ἐκ δὲ ποδοῖιν
ἄκμονας ἧκα δύω, περὶ χερσὶ δὲ δεσμὸν ἴηλα
χρύσεον ἄρρηκτον;

sentences.tr:
ē ou memnēi hote t’ ekremō hypsothen, ek de podoiin
akmonas hēka dyō, peri chersi de desmon iēla
chryseon arrēkton;

sentences.l:
and whomever I might catch
I would fling, seizing him, from the threshold, until he reached
the earth, faint with little strength;
